/* FALLBACK colour only. A sender's name is normally coloured per sender from the
   "chat-sender-title" palette (palettes.json, ChatMessageSenderHeader::setSenderColorKey()), which
   wins over this rule through a widget-level style sheet. This applies when no key is set
   or the style defines no such palette (or an empty one -- a label's opt-out).
   Reuses chat.qss's own mentionColor accent (task-message-formatting-plan.md Stage 6) -- a
   sender's name and an @mention both name a person, so sharing the hue keeps the palette
   subtle rather than introducing a new one. */
uise--ChatMessageSenderHeader #senderTitle QLabel {
color: #7A3FBF;
}

uise--ChatMessageSenderHeader #senderTitle QLabel:hover {
color: #9257D9;
}
